# The same binary with detection switched off (MEDIA_CALL_GUARD_LIST_CMD=true),
# so a detector on ANOTHER host can duck this one's speech across the tailnet.
#
# conflicts, not just requires: a host that observes already runs a full
# call-guard, which watches the hold flag on the same fast tick. Installing
# both gives one socket two owners with independent debounce timers -- they
# read each other's pause as "already paused", suppress their own resume, and
# barge-in fails intermittently. That is exactly what happened on the phone
# between 2026-07-30 and 2026-08-16.
requires: render
conflicts: observe
